{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Story 1934 test-contract card: authoritative contract = ticket ACs after signed plan review. Preconditions = fresh ticket with default empty impact, then real CLI/library/MCP writes. Production paths = subprocess  -> argv registry -> leaf FILE_IMPACT -> reducer; public rebar API -> same leaf; FastMCP tool -> public API; JSON Schema validator -> ticket_state schema. Tiers = reducer unit transition table + real CLI subprocess/library integration + in-process FastMCP contract. Observable postconditions = exact {kind, reason, paths}, persisted show state, exit 2/error text/no event on invalid input, old array output unchanged. Negative controls = undeclared default and existing JSON-array form. Collateral invariants = invalid writes leave state/event count unchanged; paths clear reason; none clears paths. CI gate = focused pytest nodes then make test. Threat boundary = CLI/MCP reason is untrusted text; validate >=10 non-whitespace once at shared write seam, never shell-evaluate it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785210609755120001,"uuid":"4bd45b86-0bd0-498f-946b-62a55c10e40d"}